# Version 2 of the dg_eu dependency graph, 2026-09-24. Version 1 and the change log are in
# licensedata/history/dependencygraph/. Reviewer: Giray Havur.
#
# GENERATED by scripts/build_dependency_graphs.py from the core graph dg_default.ttl
# (version 2) and the difference file differences/dg_eu.ttl. Edit the difference file and
# run the build; an edit made here is overwritten. The graph is complete: it holds every
# axiom and every default rule a check under it reads, and it names no graph the reasoner
# would have to follow.
#
# European Union default rules
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS LEGAL ADVICE. Each rule names the statute or the principle it
# rests on so that a reader can check it, explains in plain words what it does, and is a
# proposal for the association's legal reviewer, who decides whether it is adopted. What a
# licence means is decided by its text, and what the law of a country requires is decided
# by that country's courts.
#
# This difference adds default rules only. It removes no axiom of the core graph and
# replaces none of its rules, because no source known to the reviewer says that the law
# here departs from them; differences/README.md shows how a removal and a replacement are
# written.
#
# Two things the action layer cannot carry, and therefore does not: implied warranties and
# the consumer rules that go with them, which bind the parties rather than describe an act
# the licensee may do; and the reservation a rightholder may make against mining outside
# the licence, for example a machine-readable opt-out on a web site, which is a fact about
# one work rather than a statement of a licence.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix odrl: <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/> .
@prefix cc: <http://creativecommons.org/ns#> .
@prefix dalicc: <https://dalicc.net/ns#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix bpicounty: <http://www.bpiresearch.com/BPMO/2004/03/03/cdl/Countries#> .

<https://dalicc.net/dependencygraph/dg_eu> dct:title "European Union default rules"@en ;
    dct:description """The DALICC deontic dependency graph with default rules for what a licence does not say, under the law of the European Union and, for moral rights, which EU law does not harmonise, under the national law of Austria, Germany and France: the core of moral rights that cannot be waived in those three countries, the sui generis database right, the mining exceptions of the Digital Single Market Directive, decompilation for interoperability and exhaustion after a first sale. The graph is complete: it holds the axioms and the adopted rule of the core graph beside its own rules, and it is built from the core graph and a difference file. Each rule names its legal basis and says in plain words what it does. The rules are proposals until the association's legal reviewer adopts them. Nothing in this graph is legal advice."""@en ;
    dct:coverage dalicc:EU ;
    dct:date "2026-09-24"^^xsd:date ;
    dalicc:basedOnGraph <https://dalicc.net/dependencygraph/dg_default> ;
    dalicc:basedOnVersion "2" .

